/apps/hzt/orangepi-rtos-bench --help

RTOS-Bench - Cross-platform Industrial RTOS Benchmark Framework

USAGE:
  rtbench [OPTIONS]                    Run workload benchmark
  rtbench test-all [OPTIONS]           Run comprehensive test suite
  rtbench test-realtime [OPTIONS]      Run realtime performance test
  rtbench test-schedule [OPTIONS]      Run schedulability test
  rtbench test-stress [OPTIONS]        Run stress test
  rtbench test-cmd                     Run shell command support test
  rtbench export-result [OPTIONS]      Export results to JSON
  rtbench -L | --list                  List available workloads
  rtbench -h | --help                  Show this help message

WORKLOAD BENCHMARK OPTIONS:
  -b <name>        Workload name (use -L to list)
  -p <sec>         Period in seconds (default: 1.0)
  -t <count>       Number of tasks to launch (0 = infinite, default: 1)
  -d <sec>         Maximum duration in seconds (0 = unlimited, default: 0)
  -f <prio>        Task priority for SCHED_FIFO
  -c <cpu>         CPU affinity (0-31)
  -q               Quiet mode (reduce verbosity)
  -A               Run all registered workloads
  -G <categories>  Filter workloads by comma-separated categories

TEST-ALL OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <path>   Output JSON path (default: /rtbench_result.json)
  --no-realtime         Skip realtime performance test
  --no-schedule         Skip schedulability test
  --no-stress           Skip stress test
  --no-cmd              Skip shell command support test
  --no-workload         Skip typical workload tests
  -m, --multicore       Enable multicore tests
  --quick               Quick mode (smoke test)
  --schedule-cycles <n> Override schedule cycles inside test-all
  --util-start <pct>    Override schedule start utilization
  --util-end <pct>      Override schedule end utilization
  --util-step <pct>     Override schedule utilization step
  --stress-job <name>   Override stress job (default: all/all-quick)
  -q                    Quiet mode
  -h, --help            Show test-all help

TEST-REALTIME OPTIONS:
  -v, --verify          Run verification tests
  -m, --multicore       Enable multicore tests
  -q                    Quiet mode

TEST-SCHEDULE OPTIONS:
  --cycles <n>          Number of test cycles (default: 100)
  --util-start <pct>    Starting utilization percentage (default: 10)
  --util-end <pct>      Ending utilization percentage (default: 100)
  --util-step <pct>     Utilization step size (default: 10)
  --quick               Quick mode (fewer cycles)
  -q                    Quiet mode
  -h, --help            Show test-schedule help

TEST-STRESS OPTIONS:
  --job <name>          Run predefined stress job (default: all)
  -s <stressor>         Run single stressor
  -t <sec>              Duration in seconds (default: 10)
  -c <workers>          Number of workers (default: 1)
  --ops <count>         Maximum operations (default: unlimited)
  --method <name>       Algorithm/method name for stressor
  --opts <options>      Extra stressor-specific options
  -l, --list            List available jobs and stressors
  --quick               Quick mode
  -q                    Quiet mode

EXPORT-RESULT OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <path>   Output JSON path (default: /rtbench_result.json)
  -h, --help            Show export-result help

EXAMPLES:
  rtbench -L                                  # List workloads
  rtbench -b busywait -p 0.5 -t 10 -q         # Run busywait 10 times
  rtbench -b pid -p 1.0 -t 0 -d 5 -q          # Run pid for 5 seconds
  rtbench test-all --quick                    # Quick comprehensive test
  rtbench test-schedule --cycles 50           # Custom schedule test
  rtbench test-stress -s cpu -t 30            # CPU stress for 30s

